   "title": "The Centre's gross fiscal deficit and its financing"
  },
  "latestPeriod": "2026-27 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "How the Centre's deficit is financed: market borrowing, other borrowing, external finance, cash, ₹ crore, 1970-71 on",
  "note": "RBI, The Centre's gross fiscal deficit and its financing (DBIE report 656; Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy). Amounts in ₹ crore (DBIE serves rupees). From 2017-18 market borrowing is dated securities only; before, it included 364-day Treasury bills and the net effect of switches and buybacks (Handbook note 5). GFD receipts include disinvestment proceeds from 1991-92. Stages, from the printed table's own note: accounts to 2024-25, the revised estimate for 2025-26 and the budget estimate for 2026-27, each in its own series (suffix __re and __be), never one line. Cross-checked against the printed table (Innovation Hub export of Handbook report 210): 376 of 376 figures match."
